WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.063
Record, learn, review, audit and serve a flow,

2
00:00:04.063 --> 00:00:09.951
on the official MCP filesystem server, with the release binaries and no key.

3
00:00:09.951 --> 00:00:12.120
Every command runs as shown.

4
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.392
hoist doctor checks the binaries on PATH and ~/.hoist,

5
00:00:18.392 --> 00:00:20.932
and says what a key would add.

6
00:00:20.932 --> 00:00:22.879
Nothing here needs one.

7
00:00:23.979 --> 00:00:29.197
A folder of notes, served by the official MCP filesystem server.

8
00:00:29.197 --> 00:00:34.089
hoist init prints the host's configuration: for Claude Code,

9
00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:39.551
a claude mcp add command that puts hoist-mcp in the server's place.

10
00:00:40.151 --> 00:00:44.928
Its next steps go to stderr; the rest of this walkthrough runs them.

11
00:00:44.928 --> 00:00:49.003
A scripted agent starts the proxy with the same arguments.

12
00:00:50.103 --> 00:00:51.874
Use the agent as usual.

13
00:00:51.874 --> 00:00:55.261
Here a scripted agent stands in for the LLM:

14
00:00:55.261 --> 00:00:58.802
it searches the notes and reads what it finds,

15
00:00:58.802 --> 00:01:04.114
through the proxy, which records each session in ~/.hoist/logs/notes.

16
00:01:12.452 --> 00:01:17.517
--habit-only asks no model: Hoist counts which reads followed which calls,

17
00:01:17.517 --> 00:01:19.981
and where their arguments came from.

18
00:01:22.787 --> 00:01:26.406
A flow is a JSON file to review before serving it.

19
00:01:26.406 --> 00:01:29.011
flow-show renders it for a reviewer:

20
00:01:29.011 --> 00:01:34.222
what it may look up after each call, and where each argument comes from.

21
00:01:35.222 --> 00:01:37.794
After a search, the flow reads a file:

22
00:01:37.794 --> 00:01:41.043
the agent did so after every search in training.

23
00:01:43.859 --> 00:01:47.124
The file's path comes from the search's own result:

24
00:01:47.124 --> 00:01:50.453
one line of it, or all of it when it found one file.

25
00:01:53.685 --> 00:01:56.481
Record three more sessions without the flow,

26
00:01:56.481 --> 00:01:59.786
then score the agent's steps under it, site by site.

27
00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.997
The same request, without the flow and with it.

28
00:02:17.997 --> 00:02:21.543
With it, the flow's reads ride in the search's result,

29
00:02:21.543 --> 00:02:24.761
and the agent skips the calls it would have made.

30
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.805
With the flow, served by the proxy behind the agent's calls:

31
00:02:30.805 --> 00:02:32.620
--flow ~/.hoist/notes.flow.json.

32
00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:36.478
It has no arbiter, so the proxy decides with reach, asking no model.

33
00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:43.717
The flow log says why: each lookup's probability and its binding's chance,

34
00:02:43.717 --> 00:02:45.298
then why it handed back.

35
00:02:47.069 --> 00:02:49.856
The audit's sessions are new training data.

36
00:02:49.856 --> 00:02:54.653
Learn from all eleven, and diff the new flow against the one being served.

37
00:03:10.544 --> 00:03:13.302
The walkthrough, step by step, is in the docs.
